<!--meta {"lead": "An avatar puts a face, or the initials, beside a braider's or customer's name, so people recognise who they are booking with at a glance.", "description": "Image, initials and icon avatars in four sizes, with a status dot and a stacked group.", "pills": ["Decorative beside a name", "Status: stable"], "variants": "image, initials, icon; with status dot; group with overflow", "states": "image loaded, image missing (initials fallback), unknown person, with status", "sources": ["pages/braider-profile/default", "pages/matching-braiders/default", "pages/braider-profile/edge"]} -->
<section class="ds-section" id="overview"><h2><a href="#overview">Overview</a></h2>
  <p>Use an avatar next to a person's name: Nia's profile header, a braider row in matching results, the reviewer on a review. It helps recognition; it never carries information on its own, so the name always sits beside it. Use a <a href="card.html">story card photo</a> when the picture shows work (the braids themselves), not the person.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><b>Image</b> is the braider's own portrait. It is the default when a photo exists.</li>
    <li><b>Initials</b> ("NO" for Nia Okafor) are the fallback when there is no photo or it fails to load. Two letters, first and last name.</li>
    <li><b>Icon</b> (a person outline) stands in when the name is unknown, such as a signed-out account menu.</li>
    <li><b>Group</b> stacks up to three avatars with a "+N" overflow, for example braiders who offer a style.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="anatomy"><h2><a href="#anatomy">Anatomy</a></h2>
  <div class="ds-anatomy">
    <figure class="ds-anatomy__figure">
      <span class="avatar avatar--xl"><img src="../../mocks/assets/photos/nia.jpg" alt=""><span class="avatar__status"></span></span>
      <span class="ds-callout" style="left: 40%; top: 24%;" aria-hidden="true">1</span>
      <span class="ds-callout" style="left: 54%; top: 46%;" aria-hidden="true">2</span>
      <span class="ds-callout" style="left: 56%; top: 72%;" aria-hidden="true">3</span>
    </figure>
    <ol class="ds-anatomy__list">
      <li><div><b>Frame</b><small>Circle (<code>--radius-full</code>) sized by <code>--avatar-size</code>; the plum-50 fill shows while the image loads.</small></div></li>
      <li><div><b>Content</b><small>An <code>&lt;img&gt;</code> cropped with <code>object-fit: cover</code>, or two initials, or a 24-unit icon.</small></div></li>
      <li><div><b>Status dot (optional)</b><small>A quarter of the size, success colour, with a 2px ring in the surface colour. Never the only signal.</small></div></li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="variants"><h2><a href="#variants">Variants</a></h2>
  <p>Choose by what you know about the person. A photo beats initials; initials beat an icon.</p>
  {{example:Image, initials, icon and image with status. Next to a visible name, all are decorative (<code>alt=""</code> or <code>aria-hidden</code>).}}
<span class="avatar"><img src="../../mocks/assets/photos/nia.jpg" alt=""></span>
<span class="avatar" aria-hidden="true">NO</span>
<span class="avatar" aria-hidden="true">{{icon:user}}</span>
<span class="avatar"><img src="../../mocks/assets/photos/nia.jpg" alt=""><span class="avatar__status"></span></span>
  {{/example}}
  <h3>Group with overflow</h3>
  {{example:A group names everyone in one accessible label; the overflow count is part of it.}}
<div class="avatar-group" role="img" aria-label="Nia Okafor, Aisha Mensah, Jules Baptiste and 9 more braiders">
  <span class="avatar"><img src="../../mocks/assets/photos/nia.jpg" alt=""></span>
  <span class="avatar" aria-hidden="true">AM</span>
  <span class="avatar" aria-hidden="true">JB</span>
  <span class="avatar" aria-hidden="true">+9</span>
</div>
  {{/example}}
  <h3>Beside a name</h3>
  {{example:The profile head from the braider profile: avatar, name, location and rating.}}
<div class="profile-head">
  <span class="avatar avatar--xl"><img src="../../mocks/assets/photos/nia.jpg" alt=""></span>
  <div><p class="card__title">Nia Okafor</p><p class="text-muted">Toronto West · 4.9 from 86 reviews</p></div>
</div>
  {{/example}}
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="sizes"><h2><a href="#sizes">Sizes</a></h2>
  <p>Medium (40px) is the default in lists and rows. Small sits inline with body text and in reviewer groups; large leads a card; extra large is the profile header and grows from 48px to 64px at 768px.</p>
  {{example:<code>.avatar--sm</code> 32px · default 40px · <code>.avatar--lg</code> 48px · <code>.avatar--xl</code> 48→64px. The initials font scales with the size.}}
<span class="avatar avatar--sm" aria-hidden="true">NO</span>
<span class="avatar" aria-hidden="true">NO</span>
<span class="avatar avatar--lg" aria-hidden="true">NO</span>
<span class="avatar avatar--xl" aria-hidden="true">NO</span>
  {{/example}}
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="states"><h2><a href="#states">States</a></h2>
  <p>The avatar itself is not interactive, so it has no hover, focus, active or disabled state. When it sits inside a link (a braider row), the link owns those states and the focus ring. What changes is its content:</p>
  <div class="ds-matrix"><table>
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">Size</th><th scope="col">Image loaded</th><th scope="col">Image missing</th><th scope="col">Unknown person</th><th scope="col">With status</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><th scope="row">Small</th><td><span class="avatar avatar--sm"><img src="../../mocks/assets/photos/nia.jpg" alt=""></span></td><td><span class="avatar avatar--sm" aria-hidden="true">NO</span></td><td><span class="avatar avatar--sm" aria-hidden="true">{{icon:user|icon--sm}}</span></td><td><span class="avatar avatar--sm" aria-hidden="true">NO<span class="avatar__status"></span></span></td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Medium</th><td><span class="avatar"><img src="../../mocks/assets/photos/nia.jpg" alt=""></span></td><td><span class="avatar" aria-hidden="true">NO</span></td><td><span class="avatar" aria-hidden="true">{{icon:user}}</span></td><td><span class="avatar"><img src="../../mocks/assets/photos/nia.jpg" alt=""><span class="avatar__status"></span></span></td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Large</th><td><span class="avatar avatar--lg"><img src="../../mocks/assets/photos/nia.jpg" alt=""></span></td><td><span class="avatar avatar--lg" aria-hidden="true">NO</span></td><td><span class="avatar avatar--lg" aria-hidden="true">{{icon:user|icon--lg}}</span></td><td><span class="avatar avatar--lg"><img src="../../mocks/assets/photos/nia.jpg" alt=""><span class="avatar__status"></span></span></td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Extra large</th><td><span class="avatar avatar--xl"><img src="../../mocks/assets/photos/nia.jpg" alt=""></span></td><td><span class="avatar avatar--xl" aria-hidden="true">NO</span></td><td><span class="avatar avatar--xl" aria-hidden="true">{{icon:user|icon--lg}}</span></td><td><span class="avatar avatar--xl"><img src="../../mocks/assets/photos/nia.jpg" alt=""><span class="avatar__status"></span></span></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table></div>
  <h3>Both themes</h3>
  {{themes}}<span class="avatar avatar--lg"><img src="../../mocks/assets/photos/nia.jpg" alt=""></span><span class="avatar avatar--lg" aria-hidden="true">NO</span><span class="avatar avatar--lg" aria-hidden="true">{{icon:user}}</span><div class="avatar-group" role="img" aria-label="Nia Okafor, Aisha Mensah and 9 more braiders"><span class="avatar" aria-hidden="true">NO</span><span class="avatar" aria-hidden="true">AM</span><span class="avatar" aria-hidden="true">+9</span></div>{{/themes}}
  <ul>
    <li><b>Loading</b>: the plum-50 frame shows while the image downloads and reserves the size, so nothing shifts. In a loading list use a <a href="skeleton.html">circle skeleton</a> instead.</li>
    <li><b>Failed image</b>: swap to initials on the image's <code>error</code> event; never show a broken-image icon.</li>
    <li><b>Status</b>: the dot means "available this week" on matching results and is always repeated in text ("Available Sat 24 Oct").</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="responsive"><h2><a href="#responsive">Responsive behaviour</a></h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Only <code>.avatar--xl</code> changes with the viewport: 48px on phones, 64px from <code>--layout-breakpoint-md</code> (768px), so the profile head keeps the name readable at 360px.</li>
    <li>In a <code>.profile-head</code> the avatar and name wrap onto two lines when the name is long ("Amara Nkiruka Adeyemi-Williams"); the avatar never shrinks (<code>flex: none</code>).</li>
    <li>Groups show at most three faces plus the overflow at every width.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="theming"><h2><a href="#theming">Theming</a></h2>
  <p>Two component tokens drive the size: <code>--avatar-size</code> and <code>--avatar-font</code>. Initials read <code>--color-fg-accent</code> on <code>--color-accent-subtle</code>; the status dot reads <code>--color-success-icon</code> with a ring in <code>--color-bg-surface</code>. In dark mode the frame becomes plum-950 and the initials plum-300.</p>
  <pre><code>/* A neutral avatar for support staff */
.avatar--neutral { background: var(--color-bg-subtle); color: var(--color-fg-muted); }
/* A custom size in a reviewer list */
.review .avatar { --avatar-size: 2.25rem; }</code></pre>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="accessibility"><h2><a href="#accessibility">Accessibility</a></h2>
  <h3>Role and pattern</h3>
  <p>A plain <code>&lt;span&gt;</code> with an <code>&lt;img&gt;</code> inside, or with initials. No ARIA pattern applies. A group that stands alone uses <code>role="img"</code> with one <code>aria-label</code> naming everyone.</p>
  <h3>Keyboard</h3>
  <table class="ds-table ds-keys"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Key</th><th scope="col">Action</th></tr></thead><tbody>
    <tr><td><kbd>Tab</kbd></td><td>Skips the avatar; it is never focusable. When the avatar sits in a link, focus lands on the link.</td></tr>
  </tbody></table>
  <h3>Focus</h3>
  <p>None on the avatar. The surrounding link or card shows the shared ring.</p>
  <h3>Labelling</h3>
  <p>Beside a visible name the avatar is decorative: <code>alt=""</code> on the image, <code>aria-hidden="true"</code> on initials and icons, so a screen reader does not say "N O, Nia Okafor". Alone, the image's <code>alt</code> is the person's name ("Nia Okafor"), never "Portrait of a braider". The status dot is decorative because the status is also written out.</p>
  <h3>Contrast</h3>
  <div class="ds-example__canvas ds-example__canvas--stack" style="padding: 0; gap: var(--space-2);">
    {{pair:Initials on avatar|--color-fg-accent|--color-accent-subtle|4.5}}
    {{pair:Status dot on surface|--color-success-solid|--color-bg-surface|3}}
  </div>
  <h3>Motion</h3>
  <p>None. Images do not fade in; the frame is visible from the first paint.</p>
  <h3>Touch</h3>
  <p>Not a target. When an avatar is the only visible part of a link (an account menu), the link is at least 44px square.</p>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="content"><h2><a href="#content">Content</a></h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Initials are the first letters of the first and last name, uppercase: "NO", "AM", "JB". One letter for a single name.</li>
    <li>Use the person's own photo; never stock imagery or a hairstyle photo in an avatar.</li>
    <li>Alt text for a standalone avatar is the full name only. Do not describe the photo.</li>
    <li>Overflow reads "+9", and the group label says "and 9 more braiders".</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="do-dont"><h2><a href="#do-dont">Do and don't</a></h2>
  <div class="ds-dodont">
    <figure class="ds-do"><div class="ds-example__canvas"><div class="profile-head"><span class="avatar avatar--lg"><img src="../../mocks/assets/photos/nia.jpg" alt=""></span><p class="card__title">Nia Okafor</p></div></div><figcaption>Next to the name, mark the avatar decorative so the name is read once.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="ds-dont"><div class="ds-example__canvas"><span class="avatar avatar--lg"><img src="../../mocks/assets/photos/nia.jpg" alt="Portrait of a braider"></span></div><figcaption>Generic alt text such as "Portrait of a braider" (the matching-braiders card) tells nobody who it is. Use the name, or <code>alt=""</code> beside it.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="ds-do"><div class="ds-example__canvas"><span class="avatar avatar--xl" aria-hidden="true">NO</span></div><figcaption>Use <code>.avatar--xl</code> for the profile header; it already grows at 768px.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="ds-dont"><div class="ds-example__canvas"><span class="avatar" aria-hidden="true">Nia</span></div><figcaption>Do not squeeze a first name into the circle, or size an avatar with spacing tokens as <code>.profile-avatar</code> did. Two initials, sized by <code>--avatar-size</code>.</figcaption></figure>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="tokens"><h2><a href="#tokens">Tokens</a></h2>
  <div class="ds-table-wrap"><table class="ds-table">
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">Part</th><th scope="col">Token</th><th scope="col">Light</th><th scope="col">Dark</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      {{tok:Frame background|--color-accent-subtle}}
      {{tok:Initials and icon|--color-fg-accent}}
      {{tok:Status dot|--color-success-icon}}
      {{tok:Status ring and group ring|--color-bg-surface}}
      {{tok:Shape|--radius-full}}
      {{tok:Initials font sm / md / lg / xl|--text-caption|--text-label|--text-h4|--text-h3}}
      {{tok:Overlap in a group|--space-2}}
    </tbody>
  </table></div>
  <p>Sizes are component tokens: <code>--avatar-size</code> is 2rem, 2.5rem, 3rem and 3rem→4rem for sm, md, lg and xl.</p>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="code"><h2><a href="#code">Code</a></h2>
  <pre><code>&lt;span class="avatar avatar--xl"&gt;&lt;img src="/media/nia-okafor.jpg" alt=""&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="avatar" aria-hidden="true"&gt;NO&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="avatar"&gt;&lt;img src="…" alt=""&gt;&lt;span class="avatar__status"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;div class="avatar-group" role="img" aria-label="Nia Okafor, Aisha Mensah and 9 more braiders"&gt;…&lt;/div&gt;</code></pre>
  <table class="ds-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Class / attribute</th><th scope="col">Effect</th></tr></thead><tbody>
    <tr><td><code>.avatar</code></td><td>Base: 40px circle with initials or an image.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>.avatar--sm</code> <code>.avatar--lg</code> <code>.avatar--xl</code></td><td>Size; omit for medium.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>.profile-avatar</code></td><td>Alias of <code>.avatar--xl</code>, kept for parity with the mocks.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>.avatar__status</code></td><td>Status dot, bottom right.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>.avatar-group</code></td><td>Overlapping stack with surface rings.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>alt=""</code> / <code>aria-hidden="true"</code></td><td>Decorative beside a visible name.</td></tr>
  </tbody></table>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="sources"><h2><a href="#sources">Sources</a></h2>
  <p>Extracted from these mocks:</p>
  <ul>
    {{mock:pages/braider-profile/default|initials avatar in the profile head}}
    {{mock:pages/braider-profile/edge|long braider name}}
    {{mock:pages/matching-braiders/default|braider photo on the result card}}
  </ul>
  <p>Drift fixed during extraction: <code>.profile-avatar</code> duplicated the avatar with its own rules and sized itself with <code>--space-12</code> (now an alias of <code>.avatar--xl</code>, sized by <code>--avatar-size</code>); Nia's photo used the generic alt "Portrait of a braider" (system: the name, or <code>alt=""</code> beside it); the image, group and status variants were added from the core set.</p>
</section>
